  "final_message": "I am waiting for `npm test` to finish executing to verify the baseline test suite.\nWaiting for the test run to finish.\nWaiting for architecture checks to complete.\nWaiting for grep results.\nWaiting for git log to finish.\nSearching for occurrences of `channel`.\nWaiting for workspace check to complete.\nI cannot remove `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule [**ARCH-4**](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly:\n1. **External Contract Breakage**: Even though `channel` is not exposed in the REST [`OrderResponse`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/api/responses.ts#L6-L18), [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to the `orders.placed` Kafka topic and consumed by independent services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` is a breaking change for those deployed consumers.\n2. **Additive-Only & Deprecation Lifecycle**: ARCH-4 mandates that all event schema changes must be additive. Renaming or removing fields must follow a formal deprecation schedule across consuming services before the field can be removed.\n3. **Core Model Dependency**: The [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) factory derives the event payload from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29), so removing `channel` from the model would also prevent populating the event.\n",
